# Root .envrc — keep only repo-wide concerns.
#
# Per-app .env files (apps/<app>/.env) are loaded by each runtime itself when
# it boots in that directory: Vite for the frontends (user-client, admin-client)
# and Bun for the backends (auth-service, sync-service, proxy-service). Both
# auto-load .env from cwd.
#
# Loading all five apps' .env files into a single shell here caused
# DATABASE_URL / PORT collisions because later entries overwrote earlier ones
# (the proxy-service .env's DATABASE_URL silently took precedence over the
# auth-service .env's DATABASE_URL). The fix is to stop loading them globally
# and let each service pick up its own .env when pnpm filter cds into the
# package directory before running.
#
# If you need a particular env var visible in the parent shell (e.g. for a
# repo-wide script that reads it), set it explicitly here or export it from
# the calling shell.
PATH_add node_modules/.bin
